# Trivy vulnerability allowlist for ourdao-backend container image.
#
# POLICY:
# Every ignored CVE must:
# 1. Have a clear rationale explaining why it is an acceptable risk or a false positive.
# 2. Link to an upstream tracking issue or advisory.
# 3. Specify an expiration date (format: exp:YYYY-MM-DD) after which it must be re-evaluated.
#
# Example:
# # CVE-2026-XXXX: Busybox unaligned read, not reachable via node runtime. Tracking: #000
# # CVE-2026-XXXX exp:2026-12-31
#
# NOTE: This file is consumed by the Trivy scan step in .github/workflows/ci.yml.
# The CI workflow builds the production Dockerfile and runs Trivy against the
# resulting image, failing the build on any CRITICAL severity CVE that is not
# explicitly allowlisted below.
#
# To add a new entry, append it at the bottom of this file using the format:
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN: <rationale>. Tracking: <link or issue ref>
#   # CVE-YYYY-NNNNN exp:YYYY-MM-DD
#
# Entries past their expiration date must be re-evaluated or removed; the CI
# scan treats expired entries as active findings.

# (No active allowlist entries.)
